quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  23,105,"(They will be told:) ‘Were My revelations not recited to you, but you used to deny them?’"
  23,106,"They will say: ‘Our Lord! Our misfortune overwhelmed us, and we were a people gone astray."
  23,107,"Our Lord! Take us out of this. Then if we revert (to denial), we will indeed be wrongdoers.’"
  23,108,He (Allah) will say: ‘Go away into it and do not speak to Me.
  23,109,"Indeed, there was a group of My servants who would say: ‘Our Lord! We have believed, so forgive us and have mercy upon us. You are the Best of the merciful.’"
  23,110,But then you took them in mockery until they made you forget My remembrance. And you always used to laugh at them.
  23,111,"Indeed, I have rewarded them today for having been patient. They are surely successful.’"
  23,112,He (Allah) will say: ‘How many years did you remain on earth?’
  23,113,They will say: ‘We remained for a day or part of a day; yet ask those who keep count.’
  23,114,He will say: ‘You remained just for a little while if only you had known!
  23,115,Did you then suppose that We had created you aimlessly and that you would not be returned to Us?
  23,116,"So, exalted is Allah, the True Sovereign. There is no god except Him, the Lord of the Noble Throne."
  23,117,"And whoever worships another god along with Allah, for which he has no proof, his reckoning is indeed with his Lord. Surely, the disbelievers will not prosper."
  23,118,"And say: ‘My Lord! Forgive and have mercy, for You are the Best of the merciful.’"
